KG42.register("clusters-83f23618e03938a353ff0b0f",{"id":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v142-d-K003","paper":"16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives","label":"Coalition participation scope and the necessary cooperation conditions for investor entry","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K003","label":"Coalition participation scope and the necessary cooperation conditions for investor entry","market_meaning":"D-node consumers may cooperate with a private investor to meet electricity and heat demand; if the private investor neither cooperates with the VIU nor with D consumers, it does not enter the market. Non-MG consumers do not have the eligibility in this game to join or block a coalition, but they may still be affected by price changes. This cluster delimits participation identities and the necessary cooperation conditions for entry; it does not infer that cooperation will definitely occur or that a coalition will necessarily be stable.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["participation"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"The two chains lie within the same three-party cooperative game scope. Cooperation with D consumers is only one possible cooperation channel for the investor and cannot exclude the other channel of cooperation with the VIU; the fact that non-MG consumers lack game participation rights also does not mean their welfare is unaffected. This limited qualitative scope does not require adding numerical thresholds.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"The cooperation eligibility of consumers, the participation boundary of external consumers, and the condition that the investor does not enter when lacking cooperation jointly define the market participation scope and have independent meaning. Products, operational optimization, revenue allocation, and stability are not treated as completed results of this cluster.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Determine the cooperation choice of D consumers and the join/block boundary for non-MG consumers, while retaining the distinction between being affected by prices and having participation rights."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Supplement the condition that the investor does not enter when either cooperation channel is absent; retain only the necessary-condition direction and do not interpret the existence of cooperation as a sufficient condition for entry."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K003-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e002","v141-b-g01-E06"],"rationale":"The consumer chain describes one feasible cooperation channel for the investor, and the investor chain describes the entry outcome when both channels are absent; together they delimit the participation scope and do not add either D cooperation as a necessary condition or the inference that cooperation necessarily leads to entry."}],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G001","category":"ontology_extension","description":"R006 uses participation.prosumer to carry the private MG investor, whereas the VIU, its other cooperation counterpart, has no dedicated approved participation node; both role proposals remain pending. This does not change the current textual conditions but limits the precise expression of role semantics.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::participation.consumer","v141-c-R006::V::participation.prosumer","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g02-e002","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g03-e01"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g03-prop-utility-participant","v141-b-g03-prop-microgrid-developer"],"required_work":"Humans verify the role interpretations of the investor, consumers, and regulated VIU and handle the proposals, retaining the existing graph objects and their unapproved status."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G002","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The existing participation chain has no coalition revenue allocation, core, or Shapley rules, and coalition formation or stability cannot be inferred from participation eligibility. This is a coverage gap beyond the limited condition scope of this cluster and does not affect its assembled status as a qualitative participation candidate.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g02-e008"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g03-prop-cooperative-game-validation","v141-b-g03-prop-surplus-allocation"],"required_work":"If extended to coalition formation and stability, a source-supported revenue allocation and cooperative-game rule chain should be established separately, while maintaining semantic distinction from eligibility and necessary conditions for entry."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K003-G003","category":"unverified_source","description":"The participation conditions are assembled only according to the current unaudited candidate citations; assembled indicates that the candidate semantics of this limited scope are complete, not that the B transcription, C interpretation, or ontology roles have passed independent review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e002","v141-b-g02-e005","v141-b-g02-e007"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Humans check the original participation statements, the direction of necessary conditions, and the scope of external consumers, retaining the source's unverified status."}]},"rule_refs":["16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R005","16-cooperative_microgrid_incentives::v141-c-R006"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-a8bf79fa49226447","COMP-c0d16d0d00eebcf3"]});
